# Base URL the frontend uses to reach the backend API.
# Copy this file to .env and adjust if needed.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- NASA FIRMS active fires (optional overrides) ---
# By default the frontend reads the detections our own backend ingests:
#   GET /api/v1/fires  (see backend/app/services/fires.py)
# which needs no key in the browser, no CORS dependency on NASA, and no CSV
# parsing. Ingest them with `python -m app.cli ingest-fires` (FIRMS_MAP_KEY in
# the root .env).
#
# Set either of these to talk to NASA directly instead - useful when running
# the frontend with no backend, or against your own proxy:
#   VITE_FIRMS_MAP_KEY   a free FIRMS MAP_KEY (keyed area API, VIIRS_S-NPP)
#   VITE_FIRMS_ENDPOINT  a URL returning the FIRMS CSV schema (wins over both)
# Request a key: https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/
# VITE_FIRMS_MAP_KEY=
# VITE_FIRMS_ENDPOINT=

# --- Copernicus Sentinel-5P NO2 emissions (optional override) ---
# Real Sentinel-5P TROPOMI tropospheric NO2 tiles render by default, with no
# key, from NASA GIBS (see lib/satelliteImagery.ts). Point this at a WMS
# GetMap endpoint to serve a different/finer product instead; the frontend
# appends the standard service/request/bbox parameters itself.
#   CDSE / Sentinel Hub WMS:
#     https://services.sentinel-hub.com/ogc/wms/<INSTANCE_ID>
#   Google Earth Engine (after publishing a WMS app):
#     https://earthengine.googleapis.com/v1/<PROJECT>/.../maps/<MAP_ID>/tiles
# VITE_NO2_WMS_URL=
